Parallelize the direct-mode NORMAL advance across CPU cores, and add
frame-period instrumentation.

Applies ON TOP of linux-pinenote-7.1-hrdl-direct-mode.patch (it edits
files that patch creates); ours, not hrdl's.

Why (doc/status.md 2026-08-26 parts 11-12, measurements in
doc/artifacts/pinenote-optics-turnroutes-20260826/): the single-threaded
NEON advance takes ~18 ms for a full-panel clip at 1.8 GHz against the
panel's 12.0 ms scan period, so every page turn ran its waveform
stretched ~1.5x while pen-sized damage ran on time.  The rework splits
the advance into row-disjoint horizontal bands (the only cross-band
state is the clip min/max reduction, merged by rect union), executed on
system_unbound_wq workers with the calling thread taking the last band.
Each band enters its own kernel-NEON section; the dispatcher sleeps
outside them, so callers must NOT wrap it in scoped_ksimd() -- the four
refresh-thread call sites are converted accordingly.  FAST (the pen
path) is untouched.

Measured on glass 2026-08-26 (hand-built module, live-swapped):
full-panel frames 18.4 -> 11.9 ms (the scan period); small-clip timing
unchanged; ghost metric identical to the single-threaded path at equal
frame period and temperature bin (banding costs nothing); no visual
band-seam artifacts at 4 bands.

Two instruments ride along, both runtime-writable module params:
  - frame_period_us (rockchip_ebc): minimum frame-to-frame period, 0 =
    scan rate.  The frame-period/ghost sweep instrument; 12-18 ms
    measured ghost-NEUTRAL at matched temperature, refuting the
    "waveform timing contract" theory of the quality gap.
  - advance_bands (rockchip_ebc_blit_neon): 0 = auto (a band per CPU,
    max 4), N forces N bands.  The banding-correctness A/B instrument.

A third instrument, added 2026-08-27: dclk_rate_override
(rockchip_ebc) sets the direct-mode dclk in Hz at mode set (0 = the
33.33 MHz default).  HAZARD: the EBC pipeline goes silent at
off-design rates without matching timing adjustments (31.25 MHz:
probe clean, zero frame IRQs, no error) -- it exists to support the
slow-scan drive-energy work (the shipping stack scans ~24 % slower
per phase, the sharpest surviving explanation of its 2x-cleaner
residue), which needs dclk AND htotal moved together.  Revert by
module reload without the parameter.

